      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Raptors",
        "body": "Confusion greeted Allen Graves at No. 19, but the jumbo-wing from Santa Clara has silenced the skeptics with a summer that redefined the Raptors' forward profile. <strong>Graves saved his best for last, closing a non-consolation Summer League run with a win while averaging 16.8 points, 6.8 rebounds and shooting 50 percent from three.</strong> Fans who once doubted the pick now say he changed minds with his play, turning a questionable draft choice into the team's most promising young forward. The 46-36 finish that landed the Raptors third in the Atlantic Division feels like a distant footnote now; the real story is the momentum Graves built in Las Vegas. With one matchup remaining against the Denver Nuggets tonight, <strong>Graves will take the court again, and if he continues this surge, he could be the cornerstone of the roster's next chapter.</strong>",
